
A hello command split into a library package, its test, and a command, as one Go module.

- `mod/go.mod`: the module example.com/hello, in the directory project-hello beside the archive,
  which the node maps at the module file directory; the go command writes it,
  when the module file report of the Go module structure is evaluated;
- `greet/greet.go`: the package greet, which builds a greeting;
- `greet/greet_test.go`: the test of the package greet;
- `cmd/hello/main.go`: the command hello, which prints the greeting.

The package greet lives in the directory greet.
lib is the label of its source file, test the label of its test file.
@[greet/greet.go@`go module@=
@<lib@:greet@:Language@/Go@/File@/file@>@

@[greet/greet_test.go@`go module@=
@<test@:greet@:Language@/Go@/File@/file@>@

@<greet@:Language@/Go@/Module@/package directory@=greet@

@<lib@:greet@:Language@/Go@/File@/package comment@=
// Package greet builds greetings.
@

@<lib@:greet@:Language@/Go@/File@/functions@+
// Greeting returns the greeting for name.
func Greeting(name string) string {
	return "Hello, " + name + "!"
}
@

@<test@:greet@:Language@/Go@/File@/import paths@+
"testing"
@

@<test@:greet@:Language@/Go@/File@/functions@+
func TestGreeting(t *testing.T) {
	if got, want := Greeting("World"), "Hello, World!"; got != want {
		t.Errorf("Greeting(%q) = %q, want %q", "World", got, want)
	}
}
@

The command hello takes the name to greet from the flag -name.
@[cmd/hello/main.go@`go module@=
@<hello@:command@:Language@/Go@/File@/file@>@

@<hello@:command@:Language@/Go@/File@/package comment@=
// Command hello prints a greeting.
@

@<hello@:command@:Language@/Go@/File@/import paths@+
"@<greet@:Language@/Go@/Module@/import path@>"
@

@<hello@:command@:Language@/Go@/File@/main body@=
fmt.Println(greet.Greeting(command.flags.name))
@~ Project@/hello@/topics@/output @
@<Language@/Go@/Module@/project properties@+
module: 'example.com/hello',
@
@<greet@:Language@/Go@/File@/module properties@+
name: 'greet',
@
@<hello@:command@:UI@/Command Line@/invocation syntax@=
{
    name: 'hello',
    options: [
        {
            name: 'name',
            type: 'string',
            default: 'World',
            description: 'who to greet',
        },
    ],
}
@
